               <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{policy}_{i}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>policy</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{policy}_{i}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">straight</span>;

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{type}_{l}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>type</mtext><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{type}_{l}=</annotation></semantics></math> left-turn <span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
               Update <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{left}}(\alpha(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>left</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{left}}(\alpha(t))</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{policy}_{i}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>policy</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{policy}_{i}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">left turn</span>;

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{type}_{l}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>type</mtext><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{type}_{l}=</annotation></semantics></math> right-turn <span id="alg1.l19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
               Update <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{right}}(\alpha(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>right</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{right}}(\alpha(t))</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{policy}_{i}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>policy</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{policy}_{i}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">right turn</span>;
  
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return</span> <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}^{t+1},\text{policy}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>policy</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}^{t+1},\text{policy}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">III-C</span> </span><span id="S3.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Agent Policy</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike the original agents, whose maneuvers are specified by the dataset, the generated agents require the generators to define their action policies for producing specific trajectories.
On the discrete grid topology <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{g_{l,j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{g_{l,j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, each generated agent <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> moves sequentially from one grid cell to another according to its policy.
The grid cell currently occupied by agent <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}^{t}=g_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}^{t}=g_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is the lane index and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is the longitudinal index along lane <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.
The transition of an agent’s status refers to the joint update of both its grid occupancy and its continuous motion state:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{i}^{t},x_{i}^{t})\;\;\longrightarrow\;\;(g_{i}^{t+1},x_{i}^{t+1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.560em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.838em" stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{i}^{t},x_{i}^{t})\;\;\longrightarrow\;\;(g_{i}^{t+1},x_{i}^{t+1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is determined by the agent <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{policy}_{i}\in\{\text{straight},\text{left turn},\text{right turn},\text{lane change},\text{overtake}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>policy</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>straight</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>left turn</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>right turn</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>lane change</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>overtake</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{policy}_{i}\in\{\text{straight},\text{left turn},\text{right turn},\text{lane change},\text{overtake}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the occupancy state <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{l,j}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{l,j}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of the surrounding grid cells.
Lane change and overtaking policy are event-driven and are triggered only when specific conditions are met. In particular, we introduce a trigger time <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{trigger}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mtext>trigger</mtext><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{trigger}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for agent <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, after which the feasibility of switching to an adjacent lane is evaluated. Therefore, the target grid <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by both the temporal trigger condition <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t_{\text{trigger}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mtext>trigger</mtext><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t_{\text{trigger}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the spatial feasibility checks.
In this way, the discrete grid transition <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}^{t}\rightarrow g_{i}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}^{t}\rightarrow g_{i}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the continuous state update <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{t}\rightarrow x_{i}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{t}\rightarrow x_{i}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> are coupled to ensure that each agent follows dynamically feasible and collision-free trajectories.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.4" class="ltx_text">III-C</span>1 </span><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lane Change</span></h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For agent <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t_{\text{trigger}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mtext>trigger</mtext><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t_{\text{trigger}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the lane-change feasibility is evaluated. At this moment, the agent first checks whether there exists a valid adjacent lane <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that is parallel and allows lane-changing in the current driving direction. If such a lane exists, the candidate target grid is <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{l^{\prime},j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{l^{\prime},j}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is aligned with the current longitudinal index <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> of lane <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.
Feasibility is further checked by inspecting the local neighborhood of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{l^{\prime},j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{l^{\prime},j}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure that no existing agents occupy the target or adjacent cells, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{l^{\prime},j+k}^{t}=0,\quad\forall k\in\{-1,0,1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{l^{\prime},j+k}^{t}=0,\quad\forall k\in\{-1,0,1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Additionally, the remaining lane <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> length must exceed a minimum threshold to guarantee a safe maneuver completion.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The state transition is then defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}^{t+1}=\begin{cases}g_{l^{\prime},j},&amp;\text{if lane change feasible},\\
g_{l,j+1},&amp;\text{otherwise keep straight}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if lane change feasible</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise keep straight</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}^{t+1}=\begin{cases}g_{l^{\prime},j},&amp;\text{if lane change feasible},\\
g_{l,j+1},&amp;\text{otherwise keep straight}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-C</span>2 </span><span id="S3.SS3.SSS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overtaking</span></h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The agent scans its forward observation horizon <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{obs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{obs}}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists g_{l,j+k},\;k\leq\frac{d_{\text{obs}}}{\Delta s},\quad\sigma_{l,j+k}^{t}\in\{1,2\}\;\;\Rightarrow\;\;\text{overtake evaluation}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.560em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.838em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mtext>overtake evaluation</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists g_{l,j+k},\;k\leq\frac{d_{\text{obs}}}{\Delta s},\quad\sigma_{l,j+k}^{t}\in\{1,2\}\;\;\Rightarrow\;\;\text{overtake evaluation}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Feasibility is determined by three conditions (1) the availability of a free overtaking lane <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, (2) safe longitudinal gaps:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta d_{\text{ahead}}\geq\Delta d_{\text{safe}}^{\text{front}},\quad\Delta d_{\text{behind}}\geq\Delta d_{\text{safe}}^{\text{rear}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ahead</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>safe</mtext><mtext>front</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>behind</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>safe</mtext><mtext>rear</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta d_{\text{ahead}}\geq\Delta d_{\text{safe}}^{\text{front}},\quad\Delta d_{\text{behind}}\geq\Delta d_{\text{safe}}^{\text{rear}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and (3) existence of a continuous overtaking corridor as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\Delta s\geq d_{\text{overtake}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>overtake</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\Delta s\geq d_{\text{overtake}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">If all conditions are satisfied, the maneuver proceeds in three stages, (1) the agent enters the overtaking lane at <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{l^{\prime},j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{l^{\prime},j}</annotation></semantics></math>, (2) it continues straight within the overtaking lane at <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{l^{\prime},j+k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{l^{\prime},j+k}</annotation></semantics></math>, (3) it returns to the original lane at <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{l,j+k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{l,j+k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS3.4" class="ltx_text">III-C</span>3 </span><span id="S3.SS3.SSS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Straight, Left Turn and Right Turn</span></h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On <em id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">straight lanes</em>, agents typically maintain an approximately constant velocity, with minor fluctuations caused by collision avoidance or car-following rules, expressed as
<math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t+\Delta t)\approx v(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t+\Delta t)\approx v(t)</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the simulation step length.
On <em id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">left-turn lanes</em>, agents execute progressive deceleration when entering, maintain reduced velocity while turning, and accelerate again after exiting. The velocity profile is modeled as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{left}}(\alpha(t))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>left</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{left}}(\alpha(t)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the entry velocity at the lane entrance, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(t)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(t)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalized progress along the lane defined by <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(t)=s(t)/L_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(t)=s(t)/L_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)</annotation></semantics></math> the arc-length position and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> the total lane length, and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{left}}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>left</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{left}}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is a shaping function that enforces slower speeds in the early and middle segments of the turn.
On <em id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">right-turn lanes</em>, the maneuver is similar but with milder speed reduction:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{right}}(\alpha(t)),\quad f_{\text{right}}(\alpha)&gt;f_{\text{left}}(\alpha)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>right</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>right</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>left</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t)=v_{0}\cdot f_{\text{right}}(\alpha(t)),\quad f_{\text{right}}(\alpha)&gt;f_{\text{left}}(\alpha),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{right}}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>right</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{right}}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> imposes a weaker speed reduction compared to <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{left}}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>left</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{left}}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting the smaller curvature and shorter duration of right turns.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">III-D</span> </span><span id="S3.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Trajectory Generation</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Trajectory generation synchronizes temporal discretizations, grid transitions, and conflict management. For agent <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the dwell time per grid is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t_{i}=\frac{\Delta s}{v_{i}},\qquad n_{i}=\Big\lceil\frac{\Delta t_{i}}{\delta}\Big\rceil," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t_{i}=\frac{\Delta s}{v_{i}},\qquad n_{i}=\Big\lceil\frac{\Delta t_{i}}{\delta}\Big\rceil,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta s</annotation></semantics></math> is the grid resolution, <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the current speed, <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the simulation step length, and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of steps needed to move one grid.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The update rule for agent state is expressed as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{t+n_{i}}=f(x_{i}^{t},g_{i}^{t+1},\text{policy}_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>policy</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{t+n_{i}}=f(x_{i}^{t},g_{i}^{t+1},\text{policy}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{policy}_{i}\in\begin{aligned} \{&amp;\text{straight},\ \text{left turn},\ \text{right turn},\\
&amp;\text{lane change},\ \text{overtake}\}.\end{aligned}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>policy</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>straight</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>left turn</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>right turn</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>lane change</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>overtake</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{policy}_{i}\in\begin{aligned} \{&amp;\text{straight},\ \text{left turn},\ \text{right turn},\\
&amp;\text{lane change},\ \text{overtake}\}.\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">After each transition, the previous grid is released, the new one occupied, and the trajectory <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i}^{t},v_{i}^{t},\theta_{i}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i}^{t},v_{i}^{t},\theta_{i}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> logged.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Conflict resolution includes three cases,
(1) agent–agent conflicts, where <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=1\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=1\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> reject transition,
(2) agent–agent direct conflicts, resolved by priority rules (executing <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> pending, closer <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> farther),
(3) future conflicts, where predicted horizon trajectories <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{x}_{i}^{t+h}\}_{h=1}^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{x}_{i}^{t+h}\}_{h=1}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math> are checked for intersections. If collisions are predicted, agents adjust timing or reroute to avoid unsafe interactions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS5.4" class="ltx_text">III-E</span> </span><span id="S3.SS5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Trajectory Smoothing</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, discrete grid paths are mapped into continuous, dynamically feasible trajectories in Frenet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> coordinates.
For agent <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, its Cartesian position <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed in Frenet coordinates <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i}^{t},d_{i}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i}^{t},d_{i}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the continuous longitudinal arc-length along the reference line <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the lateral offset.
The inverse transform is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{t}=\mathbf{r}(s_{i}^{t})+d_{i}^{t}\cdot\mathbf{n}(s_{i}^{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{t}=\mathbf{r}(s_{i}^{t})+d_{i}^{t}\cdot\mathbf{n}(s_{i}^{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the unit normal at <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In Frenet space, the trajectory of agent <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is parameterized by cubic polynomials as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}(t)=a_{0}+a_{1}t+a_{2}t^{2}+a_{3}t^{3}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}(t)=a_{0}+a_{1}t+a_{2}t^{2}+a_{3}t^{3},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}(t)=b_{0}+b_{1}t+b_{2}t^{2}+b_{3}t^{3}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}(t)=b_{0}+b_{1}t+b_{2}t^{2}+b_{3}t^{3},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the coefficients <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{k},b_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{k},b_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are determined from boundary conditions including position <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, velocity <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and acceleration (derived from velocity differences).
To ensure dynamic feasibility, we further impose curvature and lateral acceleration constraints.
The curvature of agent <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s 2D trajectory <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}(t)=p_{i}^{t}=(p_{i,x}(t),p_{i,y}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}(t)=p_{i}^{t}=(p_{i,x}(t),p_{i,y}(t))</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i}(t)=\frac{|\dot{p}_{i,x}(t)\ddot{p}_{i,y}(t)-\dot{p}_{i,y}(t)\ddot{p}_{i,x}(t)|}{\big(\dot{p}_{i,x}(t)^{2}+\dot{p}_{i,y}(t)^{2}\big)^{3/2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i}(t)=\frac{|\dot{p}_{i,x}(t)\ddot{p}_{i,y}(t)-\dot{p}_{i,y}(t)\ddot{p}_{i,x}(t)|}{\big(\dot{p}_{i,x}(t)^{2}+\dot{p}_{i,y}(t)^{2}\big)^{3/2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which must satisfy:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i}(t)\leq\kappa_{\max}=\frac{1}{R_{\min}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i}(t)\leq\kappa_{\max}=\frac{1}{R_{\min}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimum turning radius.
The lateral acceleration of agent <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y}^{i}(t)=\kappa_{i}(t)\cdot(v_{i}^{t})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}^{i}(t)=\kappa_{i}(t)\cdot(v_{i}^{t})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.6" class="ltx_p">and must remain below <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y,\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y,\max}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure safety and comfort,
where <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y,\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y,\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum allowable lateral acceleration.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experiment Setup</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span>
We evaluate the effectiveness of our proposed HiD<sup id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2</span></sup> method on Argoverse Motion Forecasting Dataset 1.1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> and Argoverse 2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. The Argoverse 1 dataset contains 323,557 real-world driving scenarios, each with 5-second sequences sampled at 10 Hz. The Argoverse 2 dataset contains 250,000 scenarios, each with 11-second sequences sampled at 10 Hz. Using HiD<sup id="S4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2</span></sup>, for Argoverse 2, we generate <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="55{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>55,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">55{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> new high-density scenarios and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> additional scenarios that explicitly involve complex driving interactions, including lane changes and overtaking, as well as left and right turns. For Argoverse 1, we generate <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> high-density scenarios and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> interaction scenarios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE I: </span>Comparison of HiD<sup id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.T1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2</span></sup> with the original Argoverse 1 and Argoverse 2 datasets. For all metrics, lower values indicate more realistic and safer trajectories.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T1.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:415.3pt;height:60.3pt;vertical-align:-27.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-4.2pt,0.6pt) scale(1.0,1.0) ;">
